    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Act as a Senior Solutions Architect. Write a ultra-short, thread-style nudge for {{ $('Fetch Leads from Supabase').item.json.first_name.split(' ')[0]  }}.\n\nContext:\n- Company:{{ $('Fetch Leads from Supabase').item.json.company_name }} \n- Specific Pain Point:{{ $('Fetch Leads from Supabase').item.json.challenges }} \n\nInstructions:\nSentence 1: Start with \"Hi {{ $('Fetch Leads from Supabase').item.json.first_name.split(' ')[0]  }} ,\". Ask if they've had a second to think about the {{ $('').item.json.challenges }} automation we discussed for {{ $('Fetch Leads from Supabase').item.json.company_name }}.\n\nSentence 2: Mention that I was just looking at a similar setup we did recently where we saved the team ~15 hours a week by removing the manual work. \n\nSentence 3: Ask: \"Worth a 30-second look at the logic map, or should I circle back next month?\"\n\nSTRICT EXECUTION RULES:\n1. MAX 30 words.\n2. NO \"Checking in\", \"Touching base\", or \"Following up\". \n3. NO \"I'm writing to\". \n4. NO corporate jargon like \"synergy\", \"optimization\", or \"efficiency\".\n5. Use \"sentence case\" (no unnecessary caps).\n6. TONE: Peer-to-peer, professional, and slightly casual (like a mobile-typed email).\n7. NO sign-offs or signatures (The Gmail node handles this).",
        "options": {}
      },
